<title>FRANCE: Sagem shares down, broker downgrades.</title>
<headline>Sagem shares down, broker downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French brokerage Cheuvreux de Virieu has downgraded its recommendation on Sagem shares to a sell from a buy after 1996 results seen as disappointing, fund managers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sagem announced on Wednesday a 16.27 percent rise in net attributable profit to 638.3 million francs, but profit fell excluding exceptionals, they said.</p>
<p>Sagem shares were down 3.07 percent at 3,125 francs at 1112 GMT at the same time as the SBF 120 share index was on the rise.</p>
</text>
